WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.580
Today, I want to a quick look at how to
use a web server with Cloud Shell

00:00:04.620 --> 00:00:11.340
First, activate your Cloud Shell. Now I'm going to
make a simple web server in Node.js

00:00:11.340 --> 00:00:15.839
Here, I've pasted my code in. You can see it's a
simple hello world app that's listening

00:00:15.839 --> 00:00:20.090
on port 3000. I'm gonna change that to
port 8080 so it works better with Cloud Shell

00:00:20.090 --> 00:00:23.600
and now I'm gonna start the node
server just like you would on your local

00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:28.000
machine. At this point we can start the
web preview. You can choose a different

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:32.189
port, but I'm just going to choose port
8080. A new tab gets opened up

00:00:32.189 --> 00:00:36.050
automatically and we can see our code
running. To show you it runs in

00:00:36.050 --> 00:00:41.110
real-time, I'm gonna change the code to
say "Hello World, I'm using Cloud Shell". If

00:00:41.110 --> 00:00:45.250
I rerun my server and refresh the page I
can see the new code up and running

